rustcmd C++ - README
====================

This README is being maintained alongside rustcmd.cpp. Commands are added or
marked final only after the corresponding implementation has been compiled and
tested.

1. Build rustcmd
----------------

From the directory containing rustcmd.cpp:

    g++ -std=c++17 -O2 -Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic -o rustcmd rustcmd.cpp

The current source compiles cleanly with these options.

2. Create the user configuration
--------------------------------

Create the configuration directory:

    mkdir -p ~/.config/rustcmd

Copy the supplied example configuration:

    cp rustcmd-cpp.conf ~/.config/rustcmd/rustcmd-cpp.conf

Protect the configuration because it contains the RCON password:

    chmod 600 ~/.config/rustcmd/rustcmd-cpp.conf

Edit it:

    nano ~/.config/rustcmd/rustcmd-cpp.conf

Set the Rust server WebRCON connection details:

    RUST_RCON_IP=127.0.0.1
    RUST_RCON_PORT=28016
    RUST_RCON_PASSWORD=your-RCON-passwd

Optionally configure the Rust service unit for local lifecycle commands:

    RUST_SERVICE_UNIT=/etc/systemd/system/rustserver.service

On a Slackware rc-style system, for example:

    RUST_SERVICE_UNIT=/etc/rc.d/rc.rustserver

rustcmd honours XDG_CONFIG_HOME when it is set. Otherwise it uses:

    $HOME/.config/rustcmd/rustcmd-cpp.conf

If no user configuration file exists, rustcmd falls back to:

    /etc/rustcmd/rustcmd-cpp.conf

3. System-wide configuration
----------------------------

For a machine-wide configuration, create /etc/rustcmd and install the
configuration from a root shell:

    mkdir -p /etc/rustcmd
    cp rustcmd-cpp.conf /etc/rustcmd/rustcmd-cpp.conf
    chown root:root /etc/rustcmd/rustcmd-cpp.conf
    chmod 600 /etc/rustcmd/rustcmd-cpp.conf

This makes the machine-wide configuration root-owned and readable only by
root.

4. Installation
---------------

Installation commands will be finalised after the complete WebRCON tool has
been implemented and tested.

5. Usage
--------

The command interface is:

    rustcmd status
    rustcmd status --verbose
    rustcmd say "Hello World!"
    rustcmd server start
    rustcmd server stop
    rustcmd server restart
    rustcmd server status
    rustcmd --help
    rustcmd -?
    rustcmd --version
    rustcmd --url
    rustcmd --license
    rustcmd --config /path/to/rustcmd-cpp.conf status

6. Current implementation status
--------------------------------

Completed and compile-tested:

    - C++17 build
    - command-line command assembly
    - XDG user configuration discovery
    - $HOME/.config fallback
    - /etc/rustcmd/rustcmd-cpp.conf system fallback
    - KEY=VALUE configuration parser
    - required RCON setting validation
    - canonical project URL compiled into rustcmd
    - -h / -? / --help
    - -v / --version
    - -U / --url
    - -L / --license
    - -c / --config <file>
    - JSON payload construction and escaping
    - SHA-1 implementation for the WebSocket handshake
    - Base64 encoding for the WebSocket handshake
    - RFC WebSocket accept-key calculation
    - POSIX TCP connection and bounded socket timeouts
    - WebSocket HTTP Upgrade handshake
    - HTTP 101 / Upgrade / Connection / Sec-WebSocket-Accept validation
    - WebSocket text framing and outbound masking
    - WebRCON JSON command transmission
    - WebSocket response frame reception
    - WebRCON Message extraction and JSON string unescaping
    - non-empty Message output
    - WebSocket ping/pong control handling
    - bounded WebSocket close handshake (maximum one-second peer wait)
    - -? help alias
    - --verbose command-line option parsing
    - concise connection errors with optional low-level --verbose diagnostics
    - RUST_SERVICE_UNIT configuration
    - systemd service-unit classification and sudo systemctl lifecycle commands
    - /etc/rc.d service-script classification and direct lifecycle commands
    - rustcmd server start / stop / restart / status local service management
    - systemd server status uses systemctl is-active
    - service-management commands display the underlying service command

Still to implement and test:

    - final installation procedure
